   $q$Why is the content of the card held back until the final paragraph rather than revealed when Nadia writes it?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Delaying it shows that the card was unimportant, since the gallery nearly forgot to display it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Delaying it keeps the story in strict time order, since the card was written on the morning of the show.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-sequence"},{"text":"Delaying it hides the fact that Nadia blamed the beginner student, which would make her seem unkind.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Delaying it lets the card reach the reader at the same moment it changes a stranger's view, sharpening its effect.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Delaying it lets the card reach the reader at the same moment it changes a stranger's view, sharpening its effect.$q$, $q$Withholding the card's words makes its message land alongside the man's change of attitude, so the reader feels the surprise with him. The story is not in strict order, and the card blames no one.$q$, 'draft', '1a270ac8-ac74-5c13-b42a-385aa713cf4c')
