   $q$Why does the author include the detail that Arun "clicked the wrong button, and watched the screen go gray"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that the tracker was broken from the start, explaining why it later went silent.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"It proves that Arun is not interested in Priya's project, setting up a conflict between them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It reveals that the laptop belongs to Priya, so she must drive to the farm to collect it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It creates doubt that he can follow the balloon, which makes his eventual success more satisfying.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It creates doubt that he can follow the balloon, which makes his eventual success more satisfying.$q$, $q$The early stumble makes readers doubt Arun will matter to the story, so his finding the box is a pleasing turn. The gray screen is his own mistake, not a fault in the tracker.$q$, 'draft', '7cd89c4b-d65a-50e6-8683-4025c04e8e58')
