   $q$Why does the final paragraph shift to a single time stamp and present the ending through a photo rather than a conversation?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The single time shows that the story is ending early, and the photo replaces the data the camera failed to record.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The single time shows Ms. Ellery taking over the story, and the photo is evidence she sends to the class.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The single time shows the plots splitting apart, and the photo proves that Priya never learned who had found the box.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"The single time shows the two plots merging, and the photo lets Priya and the reader discover the outcome together in one image.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The single time shows the two plots merging, and the photo lets Priya and the reader discover the outcome together in one image.$q$, $q$After paired time stamps, one shared time at 12:10 signals that the separate lines have joined, and the wordless photo (boot, box, parachute) delivers the surprise visually. The photo comes to Priya, not from Ms. Ellery.$q$, 'draft', '7cd89c4b-d65a-50e6-8683-4025c04e8e58')
