   $q$From whose point of view is this story told?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The history teacher, who describes a student's family project","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-narrator"},{"text":"Aunt Lorraine, who looks back on teaching her niece one summer","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-narrator"},{"text":"A young narrator who visits her aunt to learn weaving for a school project","is_correct":true},{"text":"An outside narrator who knows the thoughts of every character","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-first-third-person"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A young narrator who visits her aunt to learn weaving for a school project$q$, $q$The narrator says "My aunt Lorraine" and "I came to her house in June with a plan," so she is the niece speaking in first person. We never enter the aunt's thoughts directly.$q$, 'draft', '66b84920-0178-539d-b1b0-048e495b9f43')
