   $q$How does the repeated sentence "we carded wool" affect the pacing of the third paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that the aunt forgot what she taught the day before, adding humor to the scene.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It makes the days feel slow and repetitive, matching the narrator's frustration at her lack of progress.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It introduces a flashback to the grandmother's time, interrupting the order of events.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"It speeds the story forward, showing that the narrator quickly mastered the first step of weaving.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It makes the days feel slow and repetitive, matching the narrator's frustration at her lack of progress.$q$, $q$Repeating the same short sentence for two days makes time drag, echoing the narrator's "no progress" note. Nothing indicates she mastered carding or that the aunt forgot.$q$, 'draft', '66b84920-0178-539d-b1b0-048e495b9f43')
