   $q$What does the author do to the pacing of the story in the third paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Pauses it with a flashback to Sun-hee's first race of the season","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"Keeps it the same as earlier, using the same summary of the course","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-pattern"},{"text":"Speeds it up by skipping ahead to the awards ceremony after the race","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"Slows it down by describing small details at length, though only seconds pass","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Slows it down by describing small details at length, though only seconds pass$q$, $q$"Now everything slowed" introduces a long list of tiny details (a cup, a shoelace, a sign) packed into a few seconds. There is no flashback; the details are all in the present moment.$q$, 'draft', 'b14140a3-74a6-52ca-8677-968b3cb4f4c0')
