   $q$How does the author's use of very short sentences in "Ten steps. Six. The chute narrowed." contrast with the paragraph before it?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The clipped sentences summarize the earlier miles so readers understand the full race.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"The clipped sentences speed the pace and build tension after the slow, detailed moment.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The clipped sentences introduce a new narrator who is watching the race from the sideline.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The clipped sentences slow the pace further so readers can enjoy the scenery of the course.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The clipped sentences speed the pace and build tension after the slow, detailed moment.$q$, $q$Short, counting sentences make the final sprint feel fast and urgent after the stretched-out paragraph of details. The point of view stays with Sun-hee throughout.$q$, 'draft', 'b14140a3-74a6-52ca-8677-968b3cb4f4c0')
