   $q$How does the ending create surprise?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The reader expects the story to be about beating the green jersey, but the real victory is reaching the qualifying time.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The reader expects the race to continue, but it is canceled because of the muddy course conditions.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The reader expects Sun-hee to qualify for state, but she misses the time by four seconds once again.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"The reader expects Sun-hee to lose, but she passes the green jersey in the final step of the race.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The reader expects the story to be about beating the green jersey, but the real victory is reaching the qualifying time.$q$, $q$The whole race is framed as a chase of one runner, so learning that Sun-hee "had beaten something else," the state time, is the twist. She still finishes a half second behind.$q$, 'draft', 'b14140a3-74a6-52ca-8677-968b3cb4f4c0')
