   $q$How does the author create mystery at the beginning of the story?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The box is labeled \"unknown\" and the writer signs only with an initial.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The bridge in the letters collapses before it can be finished.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The letters are written in a language that Teodora cannot read.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The night guard refuses to let Teodora stay late at the archive.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The box is labeled "unknown" and the writer signs only with an initial.$q$, $q$An "unknown" label and the single initial "T" leave the writer's identity open, inviting the reader to wonder. The guard grants the extra hour, and the bridge is completed.$q$, 'draft', 'ed175c7e-8e4b-554a-986e-8657ca6d97cf')
