   $q$How does the final detail, the mother's words on the phone, change the reader's understanding of the whole story?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It reveals the box was sent by mistake, turning the story into a mix-up that the mother must correct.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It reveals the mother dislikes the archive, turning the story into a conflict about Teodora's career choice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It reveals the letters are from Teodora's own great-grandfather, turning an archivist's routine task into a family discovery.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It reveals the mother wrote the letters herself, turning the story into a puzzle about a forged archive.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It reveals the letters are from Teodora's own great-grandfather, turning an archivist's routine task into a family discovery.$q$, $q$The photo's caption "Teodora, three months" and the mother's "Grandpa's letters" show that the baby in the letters is the archivist's grandmother, so the writer is her own great-grandfather. Nothing suggests forgery or conflict.$q$, 'draft', 'ed175c7e-8e4b-554a-986e-8657ca6d97cf')
