-- Passage rg10-literary-structure-pov-p07
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('ba38fac0-98d2-578f-91aa-780c67c15e31', 'rg10-literary-structure-pov-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-literary-structure-pov'), null,
        '9-12', $q$At the Counter$q$, $q$My father hands me the papers the way he hands me
the car keys on Sundays, already sure I will know where to go.
The woman behind the counter smiles at me, not at him,
and asks her question to the space above his shoulder.

I turn it into Vietnamese on the walk across the inch
between her words and his. I trim the part
that sounds impatient. I add a please she did not say.
He answers in a sentence twice as long as hers.

I carry it back in English and leave behind
the joke he made about the weather, and the part
where he says he once ran a shop with forty workers.
She does not need that, I tell myself. She needs the date.

This is what nobody tells you about being the bridge:
you decide what crosses. Some days I am proud of the span.
Some days I want to stand on the other side,
fifteen, ordinary, letting someone else carry the words.

On the way out he thanks me in two languages,
the second one just for practice, he says.
His English is slow and careful and completely correct.
I did not know he had been learning. I did not ask.$q$, 'draft')
