   $q$Why does the poet save the detail about the father's English for the final stanza?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It confirms that the father cannot speak English, which is why the speaker had to interpret.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"It explains that the clerk had been speaking Vietnamese the entire time without saying so.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It shows that the speaker taught her father English, so she takes credit for his progress.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It overturns the speaker's view of herself as his only voice, revealing a side of him she overlooked.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It overturns the speaker's view of herself as his only voice, revealing a side of him she overlooked.$q$, $q$Until the end the reader shares the speaker's belief that the father depends on her; his "completely correct" English is a surprise to both. She says she "did not know he had been learning," so she did not teach him.$q$, 'draft', 'ba38fac0-98d2-578f-91aa-780c67c15e31')
